      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Immediately move the truck to the coolest safe location available to slow the temperature rise. Apply any insulating blankets or cooling aids you have on hand to minimize ambient heat transfer. For food safety, monitor the internal temperature constantly—if it reaches 40°F (4°C) or higher for more than two hours, the tuna may be in the danger zone. Contact a specialized emergency cold chain logistics provider right away for an expedited solution.",
