      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While truly inexplicable failures are rare, technicians sometimes encounter intermittent electrical issues caused by vibrations shaking loose a tiny component or a hairline crack in an aging connection. Advanced electronic interference, though uncommon, can sometimes mimic tampering issues on sensitive control boards. Insist the electrician use a multimeter to test circuit voltage at multiple points, looking for momentary drops or erratic behavior rather than just outright failure. If logic fails, detailed, step-by-step testing is the only way to uncover these hidden electrical gremlins.",
